[32m+[m[32m## Architecture Highlights[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Resource-Based Authentication[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe project follows Clerk's latest 2026 recommendation:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* Minimal `proxy.ts`[m
[32m+[m[32m* Authentication enforced at the **resource level**[m
[32m+[m[32m* `await auth.protect()` used inside layouts, pages, route handlers, and server actions[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Webhook Synchronization[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mClerk events:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* `user.created`[m
[32m+[m[32m* `user.updated`[m
[32m+[m[32m* `user.deleted`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUser identity fields are mirrored exactly from Clerk while application roles remain controlled by MongoDB.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Payment Flow[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mProperty → Pending Checkout → Stripe Session → Stripe Webhook → Booking Creation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe webhook is the source of truth for payment completion.[m
[32m+[m
